## 3. Linux Filesystem Hierarchy

| Path | Contains |
|---|---|
| `/` | Root of everything — single tree, no drive letters |
| `/bin`, `/sbin` | Essential command binaries (user / admin) |
| `/boot` | Kernel, bootloader files |
| `/dev` | Device files (disks, terminals) |
| `/etc` | System-wide config files (text, no binaries) |
| `/home` | Personal user directories (e.g. `/home/temitayo`) |
| `/lib` | Shared libraries for `/bin`, `/sbin` |
| `/media`, `/mnt` | Mount points — removable media / manual mounts |
| `/opt` | Optional third-party software |
| `/proc` | Virtual — live kernel & process info |
| `/root` | Home directory for the root user |
| `/tmp` | Temporary files, cleared on reboot |
| `/usr` | Installed software (bins, libs, shared data) |
| `/var` | Variable data — logs (`/var/log`), app state (`/var/lib`), caches |

**Rule of thumb:**
- Config → `/etc`
- Logs / debugging → `/var/log`
- Your files → `/home/<you>`
- Installed programs → `/usr`
